      "value": "@{5cc8ef132dfd030ccc7c49c3|full_name}: I lead a group with around 80 people and I can say I don't recommend group leaders be mentors. I've interacted with other group leaders before and have seen firsthand how some of the groups are. VRChat seems to have it's own \"politics\" and having group leaders mentor new players just sounds like a great way for people to draft new players into their groups. I understand not all groups are like this, but a lot of the common ones I see (military RP groups) take their stuff way too seriously and get pretty toxic and would abuse this feature to grow their ranks.",
