      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I really like this idea. \n\nWhen I first joined Neos, being greeted by a Mentor, shown the basics of the game and how to get myself up and running in terms of avatar etc. was a super amazing experience. \n\nNot only that, but my mentor was super down to let me hang around with them as they went about their time in Neos helping other users saying hi to friends etc.\n\nIt immediately, within a few hours on the platform, gave me a friend group to hang out with and really solidified my experience.  \n\nIt also instilled a helpful attitude on the entire community. Maybe this is more driven by the fact that creation is mostly done in game on Neos, but everywhere I went people were helping each other and new users get started. \n\nI feel like right now most new users experience in VRChat is: join a popular world like the black cat, hear people scream slurs, chase each other around, and general chaos. If they can't handle that, they then immediately close the game and uninstall. The people that can handle that are generally the types of people who want the chaos, and if they stick with the game either develop into higher manifestations of that insanity perpetuating the cycle, or eventually find a good friend group and fall out of that \"life\" so to say.\n\nI feel like a guide program of some sort could really help with this issue. Even if it was a soft system, like a \"join guide\" option in the new player menu that puts you in a world with a guide that's \"on duty\", who could otherwise be in a public world hanging out.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
