  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So here me out:\nNew players in VRChat often have a really hard time understanding the social concept of VR and are confused about the \"Point\" of their time online. (which is clearly social interaction with fun activities sprinkled on top with friends. and other endless possibilities.) \nWhat if there was a \"VR-Guide\" system that was run by volunteers of the community. Basically, new players especially people playing for the very first time would be put in a world with a \"VR-Guide\" or maybe even a few of them, and they would sort of introduce players like a Concierge, but for your first time in VRChat.  \nThey could explain fundamentals and answer questions in a fun and engaging way. Show them avatar worlds or just hangout with them and chat!  This would not only get them socially interacting the moment that they try VRchat out for the first time, but it would also\nhelp facilitate returning players, and inspire them to explore rather than feeling lost.\nHow all of it would work, I have no idea I'm just a random artist guy. ^_^;;  but I was actually inspired by FFXIV's mentor system (allowing players that have opted to help other players basically and they receive rewards even for it.) Made me consider the concept but for VRChat.",
